- What heuristics decide when to trigger a rebuild versus continuing online?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests understanding of streaming complexity with fixed memory, practical heavy-hitter detection, and batch-based processing.

## Key Concepts
- Misra-Gries heavy-hitter algorithm
- Amortized vs per-item cost
- Threshold guarantees with finite counters
- Secondary verification for exact counts

## Code Example
```javascript
class MG {
  constructor(H){ this.H=H; this.counters=new Map(); }
  update(x){
    if (this.counters.has(x)) this.counters.set(x, this.counters.get(x)+1);
    else if (this.counters.size < this.H) this.counters.set(x,1);
    else {
      for (let k of Array.from(this.counters.keys())) {
        this.counters.set(k, this.counters.get(k)-1);
        if (this.counters.get(k)===0) this.counters.delete(k);
      }
    }
  }
}
```

## Why This Is Asked
Analyzes streaming-frequency estimation with bounded memory and batch processing.

## Key Concepts
- Misra-Gries heavy hitters; counter trimming; candidate set.
- Trade-offs: accuracy vs memory; exact counting as baseline.
- Batch processing implications on update costs.

## Code Example
```javascript
// Misra-Gries skeleton
class MG {
  constructor(K){ this.K=K; this.map=new Map(); }
  add(x){ if(this.map.has(x)) this.map.set(x,this.map.get(x)+1); else if(this.map.size<this.K) this.map.set(x,1); else { for(let [k,c] of this.map){ this.map.set(k,c-1); } /* remove zeros */ for(let [k,c] of Array.from(this.map)) if(this.map.get(k)<=0) this.map.delete(k); } }
  }
}
```

Why This Is Asked
Tests dynamic tree maintenance and amortized batch updates with range operations.

Key Concepts
- Euler tour for subtree ranges
- Fenwick/segment tree for range add, point query
